            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stoutfalcon"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Growing up, we always soaked the corn in saltwater overnight the threw it on the charcoal grill. Husks never burned, and you didnt have to add iodized salt to them. Steam cooked the corn quicker, and all you needed was butter.",
